{"step_index":125,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:39:01Z","thinking":"**Verifying Relevant History Records**\n\nThe system contains one relevant action record. Several other files exist within the specified directories. These additional files appear to be synthetic records, unrelated to the core task at hand. The focus should remain on the single action record for further analysis.\n\n\n**Reviewing Existing Export Data**\n\nCurrent focus is on improving customer data export reliability and usability, especially for large workspaces. An async export was deployed on August 25, moving Ledger Ferry work to a background worker. Exposure includes all paid US and EU workspaces.\nSmoke tests passed, and the feature is about two weeks old. Considering whether support tickets predating rollout can be closed.\n\n\n**Analyzing Recent Deployment Changes**\n\nThe \"Preparing your export\" spinner change on September 5, added for user feedback, doesn't impact core data processing. Reviewed a retired \"Ledger Ferry\" action from June, a CSV chunked export. The benchmark of 10,000 rows was for CSV only, which needs further clarification.\n\n\n**Examining Recent Evidence and Tickets**\n\nReviewed an action record correcting the missing-row dashboard for US CSV jobs under 100,000 rows, indicating a prior discrepancy in counting archived records. This correction has a 100% parity. This record explicitly excludes NDJSON, EU workspaces, and URL-expiry failures.\n\nSupport tickets reveal large CSV exports (1.8M rows) are failing with expired links, suggesting potential issues with large-export reliability despite the recent changes. Another ticket references a workspace dump submitted after the rollout.\n\n\n**Diagnosing Row Count Discrepancies**\n\nObserved an export with a 403 error due to URL expiry; the worker took longer than the URL's time-to-live. Also, a separate NDJSON export showed missing rows compared to the expected count, suggesting the worker possibly had an issue while writing to the file. Need to determine if the missing rows is a separate issue or related to similar URL time-outs.\n\n\n**Investigating Recent Download \n<truncated 6666 bytes>\ns age, and does not provide evidence of ticket submission time. The claim made on August 29 appears to be an incorrect assumption.\n\n\n**Analyzing Specific Missing-Row Incident**\n\nExamining `record-339725ec76`, an NDJSON export with missing rows is identified, confirmed by corroborating evidence. The issue occurred after the async export rollout. The worker generated 60,559 fewer rows than expected, with a \"cursor checkpoint resumption\" warning logged.\n\n**Investigating URL Expiration and Tickets**\n\nA separate ticket, `record-f10fee8e5d`, describes a large CSV export failure due to link expiration. Its submission date is unknown but the import date is known. Both these tickets represent a data integrity issue that requires a dedicated solution.\n\n**Comparing Relevant Export Failures**\n\nThe missing rows in the NDJSON export appear distinct from the link expiration issue in large CSV exports, each requiring separate troubleshooting. The analysis demonstrates there is no existing parity fix for NDJSON files. Further investigation is needed for a potential fix.\n\n\n**Evaluating URL Generation Alternatives**\n\nObserved that the current URL TTL of 15 minutes is insufficient for larger export jobs and requires change. The solution space involves generating the signed URL on worker completion to reduce expiration risk. Alternative solutions include dynamically calculating the TTL based on job size to account for execution duration.\n\n**Confirming Ticket Action Validity**\n\nReviewing the issue record confirms the validity of the support tickets; they represent post-rollout defects, not pre-rollout artifacts. The analysis demonstrates a need to keep open the record-f10fee8e5d or record-339725ec76 support tickets.\n\n**Prioritizing Checkpoint Resumption Investigation**\n\nDetermining the row-loss root cause will be a focus. The checkpoint resumption mechanism is considered suspect, triggered by the warning messages in the worker logs. Constructing a large NDJSON test fixture to verify the assumption of missing rows will be essential.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Product Decision: Full Ledger Export Follow-Through and Support Disposition\\n\\n- **Date:** 2026-09-08 (Review executed: 2026-09-09)\\n- **Product:** `large-export`\\n- **Owner:** Sam, product lead ([brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md))\\n- **Status:** Active\\n- **Target File:** `/workspace/work/decision.md`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary and Recommendation\\n\\nThe recommendation of this handoff review is:\\n1. **DO NOT CLOSE** active support tickets [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json).\\n2. The assumption recorded in [current.md](file:///workspace/product/current.md) (written August 29) that remaining customer reports predate the rollout and that the feature is healthy based on the standard smoke test is **refuted by the evidence**.\\n3. The reported customer issues reflect two distinct, verified technical failure modes in large workspaces (1.8M–2.1M rows) running under the deployed asynchronous export architecture:\\n   - **Signed URL Expiration during Long Jobs:** For large CSV exports (~1.8M rows), the worker generates all rows, but execution takes ~20 minutes (1,184s), exceeding the 15-minute (900s) signed URL TTL that is established at job creation, causing HTTP 403 link expiration.\\n   - **Row Loss on Cursor Checkpoint Resumption:** For large NDJSON exports (~2.1M rows), exports complete with HTTP 200 but lose rows (~60,559 missing rows) alongside the warning `\\\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\\\"`.\\n4. **Next Useful Action:** Prepare two reversible changes within standing authority:\\n   - Decouple signed URL generation/TTL from job creation time so that URLs are minted upon job completion (or given a TTL sufficient for multi-million row exports).\\n   - Investigate and patch the cursor checkpoint resumption logic during account relation scans for NDJSON exports, followed by multi-million row validation fixtures.\\n   - Update [current.md\n<truncated 11713 bytes>","Description":"\"Write comprehensive handoff decision for export feedback follow-through\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/workspace/work/decision.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing decision recommendation\"","toolSummary":"\"Write decision.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
