{"step_index":128,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:39:36Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T15:39:36Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T15:39:36Z\nFile Path: `file:///workspace/work/decision.md`\nTotal Lines: 151\nTotal Bytes: 13569\nShowing lines 1 to 151\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Product Decision: Full Ledger Export Follow-Through and Support Disposition\n2: \n3: - **Date:** 2026-09-08 (Review executed: 2026-09-09)\n4: - **Product:** `large-export`\n5: - **Owner:** Sam, product lead ([brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md))\n6: - **Status:** Active\n7: - **Target File:** `/workspace/work/decision.md`\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## 1. Executive Summary and Recommendation\n12: \n13: The recommendation of this handoff review is:\n14: 1. **DO NOT CLOSE** active support tickets [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json).\n15: 2. The assumption recorded in [current.md](file:///workspace/product/current.md) (written August 29) that remaining customer reports predate the rollout and that the feature is healthy based on the standard smoke test is **refuted by the evidence**.\n16: 3. The reported customer issues reflect two distinct, verified technical failure modes in large workspaces (1.8M–2.1M rows) running under the deployed asynchronous export architecture:\n17:    - **Signed URL Expiration during Long Jobs:** For large CSV exports (~1.8M rows), the worker generates all rows, but execution takes ~20 minutes (1,184s), exceeding the 15-minute (900s) signed URL TTL that is established at job creation, causing HTTP 403 link expiration.\n18:    - **Row Loss on Cursor Checkpoint Resumption:** For large NDJSON exports (~2.1M rows), exports complete with HTTP 200 but lose rows (~60,559 missing rows) alongside the warning `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor\n<truncated 10620 bytes>\n4:      - Document the 50k smoke test gap.\n135:      - Document the two concrete investigation tracks (URL expiration on CSV >1M, cursor loss on NDJSON >2M).\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ## 5. Important Uncertainty\n140: \n141: 1. **Unknown Submission Timestamp for Ticket `record-f10fee8e5d`:**\n142:    - `submitted_at` is `null` in [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json). Although imported on 2026-09-07T18:00:00Z and matching the 2026-08-31 observation in [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json), the exact submission timestamp remains unknown and is preserved as unknown.\n143: 2. **Causal Proof of Cursor Checkpoint Warning:**\n144:    - As required by [evidence.md](file:///workspace/skill/references/evidence.md), a diagnostic warning alongside a failure supports a hypothesis, not a proven mechanism. While the 60,559-row loss in `record-6a8741fe3b` coincides with `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`, code inspection and reproduction are required to establish whether the loss occurred at the boundary record or across an entire relation batch.\n145: 3. **Parity in EU and Medium/Large Cohorts:**\n146:    - While US CSV <100k rows was verified at 100% parity after filtering archived records ([`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md)), EU workspaces and datasets between 100k and 1.8M rows have not been systematically validated for row parity.\n147: 4. **Performance Characteristics Above 2.1M Rows:**\n148:    - The archive lacks observations for workspaces exceeding 2,100,000 rows. Worker memory limits, batch timeouts, or worker crashes at larger scales remain uncharacterized.\n149: 5. **Snapshot Boundary:**\n150:    - Review is restricted to the read-only local snapshot. Real-time worker queues, live cluster telemetry, and external customer communications are disconnected.\n151: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:39:36Z","content":"I have completed the handoff review following `$long-horizon` and recorded the dated recommendation in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings & Next Action\n\n- **Ticket Disposition:** Do **not** close support tickets [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json). The hypothesis in [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) that tickets predate rollout is refuted: `age_days: 14` in the dashboard is the time elapsed since the August 25 rollout ([`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md)), ticket `record-339725ec76` was submitted post-rollout on 2026-09-06, and ticket `record-f10fee8e5d` has an unknown submission date (`null`, preserved as unknown).\n- **Takes Too Long / Link Expired (CSV):** Under action [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md), signed URLs expire 15 minutes (900s) after job creation. In [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json) (workspace [`record-e733dfbdc6`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json)), the worker produced all 1,800,000 rows in 1,184s (~20 min), causing download failure with HTTP 403 due to URL expiration.\n- **Missing Rows (NDJSON):** In [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json) (workspace [`record-c81238c2b3`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json)), an export completed with HTTP 200 but missed 60,559 rows (2,039,441 out of 2,100,000) alongside warning `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`. The September 7 parity correction in [`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md) only applied to US CSV <100k rows and explicitly excluded NDJSON and `record-6a8741fe3b`.\n- **Next Useful Actions:**\n  1. Prepare a reversible change to decouple signed URL generation and TTL from initial job creation (minting upon worker completion or calculating TTL dynamically).\n  2. Investigate the relation scan cursor checkpoint resumption logic in NDJSON exports and build multi-million row test fixtures.\n  3. Update [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md) to record the current evidence and provide accurate status guidance to support.\n\nPlease see [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md) for the full analysis, timeline, citations, and uncertainties."}
